# wopcart.com Content Concept

**Status:** draft for owner review · **Prepared:** 2026-09-14 · **Language:** English (American spelling)
**Site stack:** WordPress 7.1, Twenty Twenty-Five (block theme), no SEO plugin yet
**Deliverables:** `Website/pages/*.html` (block markup, one file per page), `Website/pages/manifest.json`, `Website/product-wopcart.html`

## 0. Ground rules used for all copy

- Every product claim is backed by `digital-cart/readme.txt`, the vault docs or code under `digital-cart/src` (see the claims ledger, section 12). Nothing on the site states customer counts, ratings, reviews, certifications or testimonials, because none exist to verify.
- Spelling is American ("license", "canceled", "catalog"). The plugin UI itself uses "license" but also "cancelled"; that difference is harmless.
- No hype words, no exclamation marks. Benefit first, then the specific mechanism.
- The legal entity is unknown, so nothing names a company, address or VAT ID. Legal pages are drafts with `[BRACKETED]` fields.
- **Primary CTA "Download free" links to `/docs/`** because the WordPress.org listing does not exist yet. Once it is live, point the CTA at the WordPress.org URL and add a `SoftwareApplication` `downloadUrl`. The docs page contains the placeholder `[WOPCART DOWNLOAD LINK]`, which must be filled before launch.
- Pricing CTAs use `#wopcart-buy-single|studio|agency|pro|enterprise` placeholders, to be replaced with real add-to-cart URLs.

## 1. Target audiences and search intents

| Audience | Situation | What they search | Pages that answer |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Plugin and theme developers** (core audience) | Sell a WordPress plugin or theme with license keys, site limits and updates; often on EDD today | "WordPress software license plugin", "WordPress plugin update server", "sell WordPress plugins license keys", "Easy Digital Downloads alternative" | software-licensing, why-wopcart, docs, pricing |
| **EU creators and small software businesses** | Must charge the correct VAT by buyer country, handle B2B reverse charge and the withdrawal waiver | "EU VAT digital products WordPress", "VIES validation WordPress", "OSS VAT digital downloads" | eu-vat, plan-changes-refunds, features |
| **Publishers and course or membership sites** | Want paid posts or members-only content without losing SEO | "WordPress paywall plugin", "WordPress membership subscription plugin", "restrict content after purchase WordPress" | paywall-memberships, features |
| **Digital download sellers** (ebooks, templates, assets) | Want a light cart for files, not a full WooCommerce store | "sell digital downloads WordPress", "WordPress digital downloads plugin" | home, features, docs |
| **Agencies** | Build stores for several clients and need several domains | "digital downloads plugin agency license", "WordPress ecommerce plugin multiple sites" | pricing (Agency/Pro/Enterprise), plan-changes-refunds |
| **Page-builder users** | Build with Elementor or blocks | "Elementor digital downloads widget" | integrations |

**Intent mix:** commercial investigation (compare, evaluate) dominates. Transactional intent sits on pricing and the product page. Informational intent goes to docs, eu-vat and the blog calendar (section 9).

