## 3. Site architecture and URL slugs

```
/                         Home (front page)
├── /features/            Features overview            [primary nav]
│   ├── /software-licensing/                            [linked from features, footer]
│   ├── /paywall-memberships/                           [linked from features, footer]
│   ├── /eu-vat/                                        [linked from features, footer]
│   └── /integrations/                                  [linked from features, footer]
├── /pricing/             Pricing                       [primary nav]
│   ├── /product/wopcart/ WopCart plan product (WopCart CPT; slug to be confirmed)
│   └── /plan-changes-refunds/                          [footer]
├── /why-wopcart/         Comparison                    [primary nav]
├── /docs/                Getting started               [primary nav, primary CTA target]
├── /faq/                 FAQ                           [primary nav]
├── /blog/                Posts (section 9)             [add to primary nav after 3 posts]
└── Legal (footer): /imprint/ · /privacy-policy/ · /terms/   (drafts)
```

- Flat, one-level slugs for all pages (short, keyword-bearing, stable). Feature pages are not nested under `/features/` so that URLs stay short and survive a navigation change.
- Permalinks: `/%postname%/` with trailing slash. Blog posts at `/blog/%postname%/` if you want a separate section (set the posts page to "Blog" and use a custom structure), otherwise `/%postname%/`.
- Primary navigation (Navigation block in the TT5 header template part): Features · Pricing · Why WopCart · Docs · FAQ, plus a "Download free" button linking to `/docs/`.
- Footer navigation: all feature pages, plan-changes-refunds, and the three legal pages (add legal links only once they are published).
- `manifest.json` carries `in_primary_nav` and `in_footer_nav` flags for this. Because TT5 is a block theme, these become Navigation block entries, not classic menus.
- The WopCart store pages created by the plugin (checkout, confirmation, account) exist on the site but are noindexed automatically by WopCart.

