## 6. Structured data plan

WopCart already outputs `Product` JSON-LD on product pages and paywall markup on restricted posts, and it merges into the graph of Yoast SEO, Rank Math or AIOSEO when one is active. The site-level schema below comes from the SEO plugin.

| Page | Schema | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| All | `WebSite`, `Organization` (name "WopCart", url, logo), `BreadcrumbList` | **No address, legalName, vatID or founder until the entity is known.** No `sameAs` until profiles exist. |
| Home, Pricing | `SoftwareApplication`: `name` WopCart, `applicationCategory` "BusinessApplication", `operatingSystem` "WordPress", `offers` = `Offer` price 0 EUR (free plan) + `AggregateOffer` lowPrice 89 highPrice 699 EUR | **No `aggregateRating` or `review`**: none exist. Add `downloadUrl` once WordPress.org is live. |
| Product `/product/wopcart/` | `Product` (output by WopCart from the price options) | Check in the Rich Results Test after tiers are created as price options. |
| Docs | `TechArticle` with `dateModified` | Google retired HowTo rich results in 2023; do not rely on HowTo. |
| FAQ, and FAQ sections on other pages | `FAQPage` optional | Google shows FAQ rich results only for well-known government and health sites since 2023, so expect no rich result. It is still valid markup and useful for AI answer engines. Mark up only questions visible on the page. |
| Why WopCart | `WebPage` + `Article` with `datePublished`/`dateModified` | The date matters for the dated comparison. |
| Paywall-memberships, EU VAT, Licensing, Integrations | `WebPage` (default) | — |
| Blog posts | `BlogPosting` with author | Author entity needs a real person or the organization. |
| Legal pages | none beyond defaults | noindex drafts; once published, index is fine. |

## 7. Technical SEO checklist

**SEO plugin recommendation: Rank Math (free).** WopCart integrates with Yoast SEO, Rank Math and AIOSEO equally (`src/Seo/StructuredData.php`, `src/Seo/SystemPages.php`). Rank Math's free version includes a schema generator (needed for `SoftwareApplication` on home and pricing), per-page robots settings, a redirection manager and 404 monitor, which Yoast only offers in its premium tier. Yoast SEO is an equally supported alternative if you prefer it. Install only one.

Before launch:
- [ ] Settings → Reading: front page = "Home", posts page = "Blog"; "Discourage search engines" **off** on production only.
- [ ] Permalinks `/%postname%/`; one canonical host (choose `https://wopcart.com` or `www`, 301 the other).
- [ ] HTTPS everywhere, HSTS through Cloudflare once stable.
- [ ] Import pages, assign `page-no-title` to content pages, set the draft status of the legal pages, and set `noindex` on drafts.
- [ ] Rank Math: titles and descriptions from `manifest.json`; Organization knowledge graph without address fields; `SoftwareApplication` schema on home and pricing; breadcrumbs on.
- [ ] XML sitemap submitted to Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools; verify both properties (DNS TXT through Cloudflare).
- [ ] Confirm WopCart has set noindex on checkout, confirmation and account pages and removed them from the sitemap (view source and check the sitemap).
- [ ] `robots.txt`: allow everything except `/wp-admin/` (keep `admin-ajax.php` allowed); reference the sitemap. Decide separately whether to allow AI crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot); allowing them supports visibility in AI answers.
- [ ] **Cloudflare caching:** bypass cache for `/checkout/`, `/account/`, the confirmation page, `wp-login.php`, `/wp-admin/`, `/wp-json/`, and any request with WordPress login or WopCart cart or currency cookies. Never cache the plan API `/wp-json/wopcart/v1/plan/*`.
- [ ] Cloudflare: turn off Rocket Loader for checkout pages (it can interfere with the Stripe and Apple Pay scripts); keep Email Obfuscation off on docs pages that show code.
- [ ] Open Graph image (1200×630) for the site default and for pricing; the pages contain no images, so social shares need this.
- [ ] Favicon and site icon (Site Editor → Site Identity).
- [ ] Core Web Vitals: TT5 plus core blocks is light. Keep Manrope self-hosted (TT5 default), don't add a page builder to marketing pages, and check PageSpeed Insights on home, pricing and docs.
- [ ] Heading check: exactly one H1 per page (with `page-no-title`), no skipped levels.
- [ ] 404 template: add links to docs, pricing and FAQ.
- [ ] Accessibility: TT5 contrast on `accent-5` and `accent-1` backgrounds is fine; the `accent-3` cover uses white text. Verify buttons on `accent-1`.
- [ ] Language: `en-US` in Settings → General → Site Language. No hreflang needed.
- [ ] Publish imprint, privacy policy and terms (after legal review) **before** taking payments, and link them in the footer.
- [ ] `llms.txt` (optional): short Markdown summary linking features, pricing, docs and FAQ.
