## 10. Comparative advertising notes

- Legal frame (EU): comparative advertising is allowed if it is not misleading, compares goods meeting the same needs, **objectively compares material, relevant, verifiable and representative features** (price may be one), does not discredit the competitor or misuse its trademark, and creates no confusion (Directive 2006/114/EC, Art. 4; national implementations apply). **Have counsel review `/why-wopcart/` before publishing.**
- Naming Easy Digital Downloads or WooCommerce is acceptable only with facts a reader can check. Every competitor statement on the site must carry **source URL + date checked**; keep a PDF or screenshot of the source page on file for each date.
- **What was verified for this concept (2026-09-14, https://easydigitaldownloads.com/pricing/):** "No Platform Fees" appears in the plan cards for All Access, Professional and Extended, and not for Personal. "Software Licensing & API" and "Multi-Vendor Marketplace Commissions & Payouts" and "Physical Product Shipping" appear for All Access and Professional, not Extended or Personal. Supported sites: All Access 3, Professional 2, Extended 1, Personal 1. Prices were shown as discounted offers ("normally €999.00 → €349.65 / year", "€599.00 → €209.65", "€399.00 → €159.60", "€199.00 → €79.60").
- **Because of the promotional pricing, the site does not quote EDD prices.** Note that at these sale prices, EDD Personal (€79.60) is cheaper than WopCart Single (€89), so a "cheaper than EDD" claim would be false today.
- **Stale claims in the plugin's `readme.txt`** (not edited, per instruction): "EDD charges 3% on its free and Personal plans", "fee-free on a plan costing €199.50 per year" and "Professional plan at €299.50 per year". The 2026-08-17 figures in the vault (`Reference/EDD Comparison.md`) no longer match the live page, and "3%" does not appear in the pricing page text. Update the readme before the WordPress.org submission, or remove the price references there.
- WooCommerce: the site does not compare prices or features with WooCommerce. Its costs depend on the extensions chosen, so no representative comparison is possible without a defined bundle and dated sources.
- Re-verify competitor facts quarterly and before any edit to `/why-wopcart/`; update the "checked on" date each time.
- Include a non-affiliation and trademark notice (already on the page).

